volvement by it by the  data scientists so how does that so if  you're in the your interest is in  building a model of the data are there  different approaches that you need to be  considering between the use of a  supervised approach versus an  unsupervised learning approach well we  use unsupervised learning techniques a  lot of times to gain insight into sort  of what are the characteristics of the  data and what are the features of the  data and those will help us determine  what are the right models what are the  proper and supervised learning  techniques so that's that's one way that  these tools are used together the other  way as I briefly discuss in the case of  principle component regression is that  sometimes unsupervised learning  techniques are used in order to aid  supervised learning techniques in order  to improve the performance of supervised  learning techniques so the final model  is basically using unsupervised learning  to first reduce a dimension and then we  build a prediction model or or let's say  a regression model so so we could use  these in conjunction and use them  together in order to get a model that is  most appropriate but but the answer to  some extent depends on what is the goal  of our analysis so so if the goal is  purely prediction we could use principal  component regression and PCA together  with regression or prediction however if  the goal is to find association between  the original features and the outcome  that thing doesn't work very well  because each one of the pcs is a linear  combination of all the original features  so we can't use principal component  regression two in order to identify  which one of the out features is  associated with the outcome so the  answer to this question somewhat depends  on what is the goal of our analysis do  we want to do a good job of prediction  or do we want to find association  between the features and the outcome and  once we  that question will determine what are  the right choices of combinations of  supervised and unsupervised learning  techniques well fantastic well we've run  out of time and so we need to kind of  sign off now but I want to thank Ellie  for his talk today a really fantastic  overview of unsupervised machine  learning I want to thank those of you  who who signed in and thank you for your  questions and we'll look forward to  talking to you again next week  once again Thank You Allie enjoy your  weekend everybody thank you
 

